<title>USA: LaSalle sets self-tender proration factor.</title>
<headline>LaSalle sets self-tender proration factor.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaSalle Re Holdings Ltd said it set a final proration factor of about 67.24 percent for shares tendered under its Dutch auction self-tender offer.</p>
<p>LaSalle said the proration factor will be applied to the 5.5 million shares tendered at $27 per share other than shares that were tendered by odd lot holders.</p>
<p>LaSalle announced the $27 per share self-tender price on April 28. The offer expired on April 25.</p>
<p>The company will have about 21.9 million common shares and common share equivalents outstanding after the purchases.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
